sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: docs/reference/task-instance-workspace.md. Internal child phases only; no public container task admission.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: internal task Instance workspace phase
  %% kind: tasks.instance_workspace
  autonumber
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>parent task flow
  participant N as Node<br/>Instance runtime
  SW->>N: Run workspace phase
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - recorded Incus project and name, expected branch and head, snapshot identity and phase
  %%> - preflight returns the checkout identity; later calls must match it
  %%> Phases:
  %%> - preflight, before, after, receipt, export or discard
  %%> - check, commit or commit-ref, only from the task check child; they need no expected head
  %%> - Ansible runs workspace commands as agent in /srv/workspace; Incus stdin is closed
  alt target or evidence differs
    N-->>SW: Refuse the phase
    %%> A missing project, replaced checkout, different candidate or stale receipt refuses. Retain evidence for diagnosis.
  else phase succeeds
    N-->>SW: Return bound evidence
    %%> Snapshot trees use a temporary index. Export leaves a verified bundle in Node-owned scratch for its caller.
    %%> A check returns exit codes and Git evidence; its command output reaches only the private worker folder.
  end
  Note over SW: Remove worker scratch
  %%> Native cleanup follows success or failure. The parent discards guest snapshots only after all work that uses them has stopped, and removes the exported Node scratch after use.
